## Human intervention needed

The automated job failed in `explore/generate_tests()` while handling reporter-requested metadata. Preserved work: https://github.com/oracle/graalvm-reachability-metadata/tree/ai%2Fkimeta%2Fhuman-intervention%2Fissue-9339-fails-native-image-run-io.netty-netty-codec-dns-4.2.1.Final-79a7f8bc

The native-image repair checkpoint initially succeeded: using `UnpooledByteBufAllocator` produced 7 successful native tests. However, dynamic-access reporting then failed because `build/native/nativeTestCompile/dynamic-access` was not produced. All three subsequent generation attempts removed that allocator override to exercise `AdaptivePoolingAllocator`, but did not run tests; that path is known to fail three DNS tests with an NPE at `PlatformDependent0.safeConstructPutInt`. Metrics consequently report failure after 3 iterations, 0 generated LOC, and identical starting/ending commits.

Inspect:
